From 8939d8b5fd804a765ab14b07f3e1f5af30286ffe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nickkostik <161902345+nickkostik@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 15:55:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] backends: Embed pen ink in saved PDF pages

Save freehand ink as vector page content when a PDF has ordinary pen
annotations. Viewers and print paths that omit annotations can then
render a handwritten signature alongside the rest of the page.

Preserve special-purpose ink and other annotations. Keep the standard
save path for encrypted and certificate-signed documents.
---
 help/C/annotations-save.page           |  15 +-
 libdocument/backend/pdf/meson.build    |   9 +
 libdocument/backend/pdf/pps-pdf-ink.cc | 293 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 libdocument/backend/pdf/pps-pdf-ink.h  |  11 +
 libdocument/backend/pdf/pps-poppler.c  |   5 +
 libview/pps-jobs.c                     |   1 +
 libview/tests/meson.build              |  11 +
 libview/tests/test-pps-ink-save.cc     | 237 ++++++++++++++++++++
 meson.build                            |   3 +-
 9 files changed, 579 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 libdocument/backend/pdf/pps-pdf-ink.cc
 create mode 100644 libdocument/backend/pdf/pps-pdf-ink.h
 create mode 100644 libview/tests/test-pps-ink-save.cc

diff --git a/help/C/annotations-save.page b/help/C/annotations-save.page
index bb78dbe..65cec5b 100644
--- a/help/C/annotations-save.page
+++ b/help/C/annotations-save.page
@@ -22,9 +22,7 @@
 </info>
 <title>Save a copy of an annotated PDF</title>
  <p>
-  To save a copy of your annotated PDF for future viewing using the
-  <app>Document Viewer</app> or any other PDF viewer
-  <em>that supports annotations</em>:
+  Use <app>Document Viewer</app> to save a copy of your PDF edits.
  </p>
   <steps>
    <item>
@@ -40,8 +38,15 @@
     </item>
    </steps>
    <p>
-   Annotations are added according to the PDF specification. Therefore, most PDF
-   readers should be able to read them. Adobe Reader is known to work.
+   When you save a PDF with plain pen strokes, the strokes become part of
+   the page so they remain visible in other viewers and when printed. To keep
+   the original page, save to a new file. Once you open the saved copy, you
+   can no longer erase those strokes with the annotation tools.
+   </p>
+   <p>
+   Password-protected PDFs and PDFs with certificate signatures keep their
+   editable annotations. Other annotations require a viewer that supports
+   them.
    </p>
 
 </page>
